From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/dovi_rpudec, avutil/dovi_meta: keep each DM extension
 block's bytes

The Dolby Vision tunnel sends a title's display management metadata on
to the TV. FFmpeg parses each extension block of the RPU into
AVDOVIDmData, and the output stage cannot rebuild every block from the
parsed fields (CM v4.0 metadata in particular).

Keep the block's original payload next to the parsed fields:
AVDOVIDmData gains dvbridge_raw_magic (0x41424456 when the bytes are
there), dvbridge_original_length and dvbridge_original_bytes[32]. The
bytes are the bit-packed RPU payload of the block, read through a copy
of the bit reader, not HDMI payload bytes. A block whose stated length
runs past the end of the data is refused (AVERROR_INVALIDDATA) before
anything is copied; a block longer than 32 bytes keeps its length and no
bytes.

The fields are at the end of AVDOVIDmData. They change the size of a
public struct, so this FFmpeg and the player have to be built together
(Kodi's Dolby Vision code reads them).

Origin: the native-dv Kodi port (yblod-engine), "dvbridge".

Regrouped from ffmpeg-9900-00-libavcodec__dovi_rpudec.c and
ffmpeg-9900-02-libavutil__dovi_meta.h, one change split per source file
(YBLOD 0.2 to 0.4.1); no code change.
---
 libavcodec/dovi_rpudec.c | 11 +++++++++++
 libavutil/dovi_meta.h    |  5 +++++
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libavcodec/dovi_rpudec.c b/libavcodec/dovi_rpudec.c
index 00005049be17..f7fa9e128fcd 100644
--- a/libavcodec/dovi_rpudec.c
+++ b/libavcodec/dovi_rpudec.c
@@ -319,6 +319,17 @@ static int parse_ext_blocks(DOVIContext *s, GetBitContext *gb, int ver,
 
         memset(dm, 0, sizeof(*dm));
         dm->level = level;
+        /* Validate before copying from the bitreader, including non-byte-aligned
+         * block starts. Static/compressed state inherits this trailer naturally. */
+        if (ext_block_length < 0 || ext_block_length > get_bits_left(gb) / 8)
+            return AVERROR_INVALIDDATA;
+        dm->dvbridge_original_length = ext_block_length;
+        if (ext_block_length <= sizeof(dm->dvbridge_original_bytes)) {
+            GetBitContext raw = *gb;
+            for (int j = 0; j < ext_block_length; j++)
+                dm->dvbridge_original_bytes[j] = get_bits(&raw, 8);
+            dm->dvbridge_raw_magic = 0x41424456;
+        }
         switch (ver) {
         case 1: ret = parse_ext_v1(s, gb, dm); break;
         case 2: ret = parse_ext_v2(s, gb, dm, ext_block_length); break;
diff --git a/libavutil/dovi_meta.h b/libavutil/dovi_meta.h
index c102bf384f46..598d2440f1f4 100644
--- a/libavutil/dovi_meta.h
+++ b/libavutil/dovi_meta.h
@@ -332,6 +332,11 @@ typedef struct AVDOVIDmData {
         AVDOVIDmLevel254 l254; /* static */
         AVDOVIDmLevel255 l255; /* static */
     };
+    /* Dvbridge isolated-lab trailer. Preserve presence even when value is zero.
+     * Original RPU block bytes are bit-packed, NOT HDMI payload bytes. */
+    uint32_t dvbridge_raw_magic;
+    uint32_t dvbridge_original_length;
+    uint8_t dvbridge_original_bytes[32];
 } AVDOVIDmData;
 
 /**
